Trying not to make any abrupt movements, you carefully take the canister with herbicide using the free hand, take out the stopper with the help of your teeth and shower the predatory branch stuck to your arm. The fuzz, covered with shining drops, begin to turn dark and shrink before your eyes, but the terrible stubborn plant keeps holding you. Quite a lot of time has passed, before the substance finally kills the clammy fuzz, stuck to your arm. You step back very carefully and fall powerlessly on the grass, gasping for some air.
When you recover completely, you go back. Now it is clear, that path through the lilac plants is deadly dangerous, so you have no other option, but to make your way through the thick shrubs of white flower bushes.